\section{Recommended linking route}{

Before fitting, use \code{\link[=describe_mfrm_data]{describe_mfrm_data()}} on the rating table and inspect
\code{design_connectivity}. Supply \code{expected_design} if the planned assignment
is available, so unassigned cells and missing assigned ratings are distinct.
A connected graph alone does not establish identification of all model
parameters, adequate precision, or absence of informative assignment.
\enumerate{
\item Fit with \code{\link[=fit_mfrm]{fit_mfrm()}} and diagnose with \code{\link[=diagnose_mfrm]{diagnose_mfrm()}}.
\item Check connectedness with \code{\link[=subset_connectivity_report]{subset_connectivity_report()}}.
\item Build or review anchors with \code{\link[=make_anchor_table]{make_anchor_table()}} and
\code{\link[=review_mfrm_anchors]{review_mfrm_anchors()}}.
\item Use \code{\link[=anchor_to_baseline]{anchor_to_baseline()}} when you need to place raw new data onto a
baseline scale.
\item Use \code{\link[=build_equating_chain]{build_equating_chain()}} only as a screened linking aid across
already fitted waves.
\item Use \code{\link[=detect_anchor_drift]{detect_anchor_drift()}} for stability monitoring on separately fitted
waves.
\item Use \code{\link[=build_linking_review]{build_linking_review()}} when you need one operational synthesis
object rather than separate anchor/drift/chain tables.
\item Run \code{\link[=analyze_dff]{analyze_dff()}} only after checking connectivity and common-scale
evidence.
}
